<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/06/01 - July MVP Feature Refinement, Module=
 Division of Labor, and Subsequent Action Items</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"67b469a994a6">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"e54650a4d6ea">Thank you so much for your attendance. Please =
kindly check the meeting minutes below for the meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ec7ecd005c53">Date: Monday, 1st June, 2026</p>
<p local-id=3D"7025e64c0ea9">Time: 17:30&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"e72c0b503d2a">Attendees: Tao Huang, Loura Guo, Jiajin Zhong,=
 Daijiang Xie, Yixi Wang, Suijie Song, Guangyuan Mu, Huifang Liu, Jiaxing D=
ai</p>
<hr local-id=3D"7e912723-2995-4cda-9071-09ed4913b3eb">
<h2 local-id=3D"b964d699f5e0" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/01-JulyMVPFeatu=
reRefinement,ModuleDivisionofLabor,andSubsequentActionItems-QuickRecap">Qui=
ck Recap</h2>
<p local-id=3D"a72469a0dad4">This meeting is the fourth weekly meeting of t=
he =E6=B1=87=E4=B8=B0=E7=A7=91=E6=8A=80=E8=8F=81=E8=8B=B1=E8=AE=AD=E7=BB=83=
=E8=90=A5 =E2=80=93 AI=E6=99=BA=E8=83=BD=E9=97=AE=E7=AD=94=E5=8A=A9=E6=89=
=8B.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7916aaf2b75f">In this meeting, Jiajin shared some AI knowled=
ge about Graph RAG and discussed its differences from traditional RAG. The =
team then reviewed the progress of last week=E2=80=99s action items, includ=
ing the Confluence usage standard, the Q1 timeline, and the functional desi=
gn of each system layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3fa31b1c20ad">The team further clarified the major modules o=
f the Q&amp;A system, including the data processing pipeline, data persiste=
nce layer, tool set, agent layer, and user layer. Mentors also provided fee=
dback on the system architecture diagram, timeline planning, documentation =
standard, and team collaboration approach.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"b9827a17-3388-4b48-8491-37a115a72b5d">
<h2 local-id=3D"a9aed79fdcc1" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/01-JulyMVPFeatu=
reRefinement,ModuleDivisionofLabor,andSubsequentActionItems-DiscussionSumma=
ry">Discussion Summary</h2>
<p local-id=3D"668c97569f7e">Jiajin shared the concept of Graph RAG and exp=
lained that it is more suitable for questions involving entities, relations=
hips, and multi-hop reasoning. The team discussed that Graph RAG may be hel=
pful for relationship-based queries, but it may also introduce higher token=
 cost, slower retrieval, and maintenance difficulties when the graph needs =
frequent updates.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3cbaf2666100">Yixi introduced the current Confluence setup. =
Four Confluence spaces have been prepared for different groups, and each sp=
ace includes a usage guide. The team discussed the need to divide documents=
 into relatively stable documents and continuously updated documents, so th=
at future synchronization between Confluence and the local knowledge base c=
an be tested more clearly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"48245e96c27a">The team discussed two possible collaboration =
models. One option is to divide work by module, so each subgroup focuses on=
 a specific system layer. The other option is to let all members participat=
e in multiple modules, so that everyone can understand the whole project be=
tter. After discussion, the team tentatively agreed to first proceed by mod=
ule-based division for efficiency, and later allow members with extra capac=
ity to support other modules.</p>
<p local-id=3D"23e067ad9702">Guangyuan presented the data processing pipeli=
ne. This layer is responsible for parsing documents, extracting document st=
ructures, building section trees, splitting content into chunks, preserving=
 title paths, and preparing structured JSON output. The team also discussed=
 the possibility of using mature document parsing APIs or tools in the futu=
re if the basic parser is not sufficient.</p>
<p local-id=3D"db913d50d564">Jiajin presented the embedding and storage par=
t of the data processing pipeline. This part includes selecting and configu=
ring an embedding model, implementing single-text and batch-text vectorizat=
ion functions, and calling the data persistence layer to store vectors, ori=
ginal text, document IDs, chunk indexes, and local JSON files.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ddbf01aa25e1">Guangyuan also introduced the tool set layer. =
The tool set acts as the bridge between the agent layer and the data persis=
tence layer. The current Q1 focus is the search tool, which should support =
semantic vector retrieval, BM25 retrieval, hybrid retrieval, top-k control,=
 score threshold filtering, and metadata filtering.</p>
<p local-id=3D"88792d9614c4">Huifang and Suijie presented the agent layer. =
The agent layer receives the user question, validates the input, generates =
a trace ID, calls the retrieval tool, assembles the prompt, calls the LLM, =
generates the answer, returns citations, and handles exceptional cases. The=
 Q1 agent will focus on a single-turn RAG agent rather than a complex multi=
-agent or multi-turn system.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2573cf1557c3">Jiaxing and Daijiang presented the user layer.=
 Jiaxing focused on the basic web page, chat interface, input box, message =
display, loading state, and streaming display effect. Daijiang focused on t=
he interface connection between the web layer and the agent layer, includin=
g Agent API calling, response parsing, status mapping, streaming token hand=
ling, error display, mock data, and mock API for independent frontend testi=
ng.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9b5e5c5282e3">Tao suggested that the system architecture dia=
gram should be further optimized. The diagram should clearly show what each=
 layer needs to achieve for Checkpoint 1, while detailed implementation cho=
ices such as specific vector databases or retrieval algorithms can be left =
in separate documents.</p>
<p local-id=3D"32037d505bb7">Loura suggested that, in addition to the Q1 ti=
meline, the team should also prepare an overall project timeline slide. She=
 also reminded the MoM noter to attach the one-page slide and the Confluenc=
e page standard to the meeting minutes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f8e8ec3b7b2f">Tao also suggested that project documents shou=
ld be written in English as much as possible, since HSBC is an internationa=
l company and most internal documents are usually written in English.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"0f648955-c1fa-48e9-8180-a433b87d9cfc">
<h2 local-id=3D"28851a609950" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/01-JulyMVPFeatu=
reRefinement,ModuleDivisionofLabor,andSubsequentActionItems-ActionItems">Ac=
tion Items</h2>
<p local-id=3D"ae13d6d86b87">All team members: Continue implementation base=
d on the module-based division of work.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a64a16ff0ba4">All team members: Further clarify the owner of=
 each function point and make sure every function has a responsible person.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"b371d800cf25">All team members: Continue improving the Q1 / =
Checkpoint 1 design based on the layered architecture, including data proce=
ssing pipeline, data persistence layer, tool set, agent layer, and user lay=
er.</p>
<p local-id=3D"db99918e8426">All team members: Try to write project documen=
ts in English as much as possible.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e4e1dd194a0f">Yixi and related team members: Finalize and sh=
are the Confluence usage standard, including document structure, naming con=
ventions, templates, and maintenance mechanism.</p>
<p local-id=3D"95e643bcfbdd">Yixi and related team members: Share the Feish=
u document link with the team.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0c6d9ea01e81">Yixi and related team members: Prepare or upda=
te the one-page timeline PPT, including key milestones, deliverables, depen=
dencies, and risks.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb02b4a4daaa">Yixi and related team members: Prepare an over=
all project timeline slide in addition to the Q1 timeline.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9bf87c47e108">Team members responsible for the architecture =
design: Optimize the system architecture diagram so that each layer=E2=80=
=99s Checkpoint 1 functions are clear at a glance.</p>
<p local-id=3D"28c31f1c7d7c">Data processing pipeline team: Continue workin=
g on document parsing, section tree construction, chunking strategy, JSON o=
utput, and BM25 index preparation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"da10775b9c42">Embedding and storage related members: Continu=
e working on embedding model configuration, single-text and batch-text vect=
orization, vector storage, and local document storage.</p>
<p local-id=3D"16840b905a25">Tool set team: Continue implementing the searc=
h tool, including vector retrieval, BM25 retrieval, hybrid retrieval, top-k=
 control, threshold filtering, and metadata filtering.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d85167d4731f">Agent layer team: Continue working on input va=
lidation, trace ID generation, retrieval tool calling, prompt assembly, LLM=
 calling, answer generation, citation return, logging, and fallback handlin=
g.</p>
<p local-id=3D"14cf51d06e3b">User layer team: Continue working on the chat =
page, Agent API calling, response parsing, status mapping, streaming output=
, mock data, mock API, and frontend-Agent integration.</p>
<p local-id=3D"158a685af51a">Daijiang: Prepare and send out the meeting min=
utes. Please attach the one-page slide and the Confluence page standard if =
available.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"b2b89fba-68bb-41ea-add4-da60b2976570">
<h2 local-id=3D"3eeaffbe73a2" id=3D"MeetingMinutesof2026/06/01-JulyMVPFeatu=
reRefinement,ModuleDivisionofLabor,andSubsequentActionItems-Attachments">At=
tachments</h2>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"5ac27b9c-3ac0-487d-b530-f1be36bd8af8">
<li local-id=3D"211f3525-d20a-48f2-a252-5e93de2f1f57">
<p local-id=3D"c24e6c4e3fde">One-page timeline slide&nbsp;</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"94fafab0-3c24-4d31-a9f9-e33fc7fe62b1">
<p local-id=3D"0aac9a99e115">Confluence page standard&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"af5f4a33d21b"></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
